{{!
    @template theme_erasight/hero

    The front-page hero banner. New, theme-owned markup — not a core
    override, so there was nothing to verify markup against; only the data
    (headline pieces, cta urls, stats) needed real Moodle APIs, all built
    in layout/frontpage.php.

    Context: eyebrow (a small label above the headline), headlinepre/
    headlineemphasis/headlinepost (three pieces of one headline sentence,
    split so the middle piece can be styled distinctly), tagline, cta (an
    object with primaryurl/primarylabel/secondaryurl/secondarylabel), and
    stats (an array of value/label — real course and teammate counts, not
    fabricated).

    NOTE: never write two closing-brace characters next to each other
    anywhere in this comment block — a Mustache comment ends at the first
    such occurrence it scans past, not a matched one, which is why this
    comment is prose rather than a literal JSON/tag example.
}}
<div class="erasight-hero">
    <div class="erasight-hero-inner">
        <div class="erasight-hero-eyebrow">{{eyebrow}}</div>
        <h1 class="erasight-hero-title">{{headlinepre}}<span class="erasight-emphasis">{{headlineemphasis}}</span>{{headlinepost}}</h1>
        <p class="erasight-hero-tagline">{{tagline}}</p>
        <div class="erasight-hero-cta">
            <a class="erasight-hero-btn erasight-hero-btn-primary" href="{{cta.primaryurl}}">{{cta.primarylabel}}</a>
            <a class="erasight-hero-btn erasight-hero-btn-secondary" href="{{cta.secondaryurl}}">{{cta.secondarylabel}}</a>
        </div>
        <div class="erasight-hero-stats">
            {{#stats}}
            <div class="erasight-hero-stat">
                <span class="erasight-hero-stat-value">{{value}}</span>
                <span class="erasight-hero-stat-label">{{label}}</span>
            </div>
            {{/stats}}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
